DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       hhoosstt is a simple utility for performing DNS  lookups.  It  is  normally
       used to convert names to IP addresses and vice versa. When no arguments
       or  options  are given, hhoosstt prints a short summary of its command-line
       arguments and options.

       nnaammee is the domain name that is to be looked up. It can also be a  dot‐
       ted-decimal  IPv4  address  or a colon-delimited IPv6 address, in which
       case hhoosstt by default  performs  a  reverse  lookup  for  that  address.
       sseerrvveerr  is  an optional argument which is either the name or IP address
       of the name server that hhoosstt should query  instead  of  the  server  or
       servers listed in //eettcc//rreessoollvv..ccoonnff.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --44     This  option  specifies  that only IPv4 should be used for query
              transport. See also the _-_6 option.

       --66     This option specifies that only IPv6 should be  used  for  query
              transport. See also the _-_4 option.

       --aa     The  _-_a  ("all")  option is normally equivalent to _-_v _-_t _A_N_Y. It
              also affects the behavior of the _-_l list zone option.

       --AA     The _-_A ("almost all") option is equivalent to  _-_a,  except  that
              RRSIG, NSEC, and NSEC3 records are omitted from the output.

       --cc ccllaassss
              This  option  specifies  the  query  class, which can be used to
              lookup HS (Hesiod) or CH (Chaosnet) class resource records.  The
              default class is IN (Internet).

       --CC     This option indicates that _n_a_m_e_d should check consistency, mean‐
              ing that hhoosstt queries the SOA records for zone nnaammee from all the
              listed  authoritative  name  servers  for that zone. The list of
              name servers is defined by the NS records that are found for the
