       --dd     This option prints debugging traces, and is equivalent to the _-_v
              verbose option.

       --ll     This option tells _n_a_m_e_d to list the zone, meaning the hhoosstt  com‐
              mand  performs  a  zone transfer of zone nnaammee and prints out the
              NS, PTR, and address records (A/AAAA).

              Together, the _-_l _-_a options print all records in the zone.

       --NN nnddoottss
              This option specifies the number of dots (nnddoottss) that have to be
              in nnaammee for it to be considered absolute. The default  value  is
              that defined using the nnddoottss statement in //eettcc//rreessoollvv..ccoonnff, or 1
              if  no nnddoottss statement is present. Names with fewer dots are in‐
              terpreted as relative names, and are searched for in the domains
              listed in the sseeaarrcchh or ddoommaaiinn directive in //eettcc//rreessoollvv..ccoonnff.

       --pp ppoorrtt
              This option specifies the port to query on the server.  The  de‐
              fault is 53.

       --rr     This option specifies a non-recursive query; setting this option
              clears  the  RD (recursion desired) bit in the query. This means
              that the name server receiving the query does not attempt to re‐
              solve nnaammee. The _-_r option enables hhoosstt to mimic the behavior  of
              a  name server by making non-recursive queries, and expecting to
              receive answers to those queries that can be referrals to  other
