IIDDNN SSUUPPPPOORRTT
       If hhoosstt has been built with IDN (internationalized  domain  name)  sup‐
       port,  it can accept and display non-ASCII domain names. hhoosstt appropri‐
       ately converts character encoding of a domain name before sending a re‐
       quest to a DNS server or displaying a reply from the server.   To  turn
       off  IDN support, define the IIDDNN__DDIISSAABBLLEE environment variable. IDN sup‐
       port is disabled if the variable is set when hhoosstt runs.

